 "notes": "Curve digitised from Fig. 1 (Plots/YoungGCFiducialCond.jpeg in the arXiv e-print): the thick dark-red solid line, i.e. the median 95% CL upper limit on |g_agamma| over 100 MC realizations of the Galactic Center neutron-star population (fiducial 'Young' NS model conditioned on the observed GC magnetar). Extracted by color segmentation of the raster figure; axes calibrated against tick marks (x log-scale in m_a from 15-35 ueV, y log-scale 1e-15 to ~2e-10 GeV^-1). Curve spans ~16.6-31.9 ueV (GBT C-band 4-8 GHz); a short segment near 16.7-17.05 ueV where the limit rises above the plotted range is omitted. Narrow RFI-veto spikes are partially smoothed by a 5-column median filter. The paper writes L = g a E.B, identical to the canonical -(g/4) a F Fdual. Signal assumes an NFW halo (scale radius 20 kpc) normalized to a local DM density of 0.346 GeV/cm^3; no density rescaling applied. The 68%/95% population-model containment bands were not extracted.",
